1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,714
Some jobs are best done by a specialist.

2
00:00:03,714 --> 00:00:08,728
This video shows how Agent profiles let your assistants hand work to specialist

3
00:00:08,728 --> 00:00:13,801
agents, how your site offers its agents to other systems over the Agent-to-Agent

4
00:00:13,801 --> 00:00:17,340
protocol, and how to use the agents of another system.

5
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:25,732
An assistant that does everything is hard to maintain.

6
00:00:25,732 --> 00:00:29,840
Its instructions grow, and its answers become less focused.

7
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:35,196
A specialist agent has one job, its own instructions and its own tools,

8
00:00:35,196 --> 00:00:37,050
so it does that job well.

9
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:45,860
The Agent-to-Agent protocol, or A2A, lets agents on different systems find each other and work together.

10
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:50,657
Your site can offer its agents to other systems, and your assistants can

11
00:00:50,657 --> 00:00:52,680
call the agents of other systems.

12
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:01,066
An agent is an AI profile of type Agent, with a description that

13
00:01:01,066 --> 00:01:02,860
says what it is good at.

14
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:10,243
The A2A Host feature offers every Agent profile to other systems, which discover

15
00:01:10,243 --> 00:01:13,020
them in the site's agent card.

16
00:01:13,770 --> 00:01:19,163
The A2A Client feature adds connections to the hosts of other systems, and

17
00:01:19,163 --> 00:01:23,950
each agent they offer becomes something your assistants can call.

18
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:28,013
Each part is its own feature, so you only see the menus of

19
00:01:28,013 --> 00:01:29,980
the features that are turned on.

20
00:01:34,181 --> 00:01:38,678
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, and click Add Profile.

21
00:01:38,678 --> 00:01:42,978
In the New AI Profile window, click Start on Blank profile.

22
00:01:42,978 --> 00:01:47,211
The other cards are ready-made profiles, including agents.

23
00:01:47,662 --> 00:01:51,020
Enter a Title, and set the Profile type to Agent.

24
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:54,072
The Description and the Availability appear.

25
00:01:54,548 --> 00:01:57,411
Write the Description for the other assistants.

26
00:01:57,411 --> 00:02:00,975
It says exactly what the agent does and when to call it, and

27
00:02:00,975 --> 00:02:02,488
it is how they decide.

28
00:02:02,944 --> 00:02:06,370
Availability decides when the agent is included.

29
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:10,051
On demand includes it only when it fits the request.

30
00:02:10,051 --> 00:02:14,874
Always available includes it in every request, which uses more tokens.

31
00:02:15,329 --> 00:02:19,324
Under System instructions, tell the agent how to behave.

32
00:02:19,324 --> 00:02:20,419
Click Save.

33
00:02:24,619 --> 00:02:31,509
With the Agent-to-Agent Host feature on, your site offers every Agent profile to other systems.

34
00:02:32,259 --> 00:02:37,709
Other systems discover the agents from the site's agent card, and send them messages.

35
00:02:38,459 --> 00:02:42,201
Your technical team chooses how callers sign in:

36
00:02:42,201 --> 00:02:46,359
no sign-in for testing, an API key, or OpenID Connect.

37
00:02:47,109 --> 00:02:53,809
When the host asks for it, a caller also needs the Access the A2A Host permission.

38
00:02:57,987 --> 00:03:03,095
To use the agents of another system, open Artificial Intelligence, Agent to Agent

39
00:03:03,095 --> 00:03:05,327
Hosts, and click Add Connection.

40
00:03:05,777 --> 00:03:13,154
Enter a Title, and the Endpoint, which is the address of the other system's A2A host.

41
00:03:13,154 --> 00:03:19,477
Here the host runs on this machine, and its address ends with slash A2A.

42
00:03:19,934 --> 00:03:25,162
Authentication offers the same choices as an MCP connection:

43
00:03:25,162 --> 00:03:32,450
Anonymous, API Key, Basic Authentication, three OAuth 2.0 options, and Custom Headers.

44
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:36,014
Anonymous suits an open host or a test.

45
00:03:36,468 --> 00:03:37,449
Click Save.

46
00:03:37,449 --> 00:03:42,758
The site reads the agent card of the host when an assistant first uses the connection.

47
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:51,534
Open the profile of an assistant, and its Capabilities tab.

48
00:03:51,534 --> 00:03:54,989
Under A2A Connections, tick the connection.

49
00:03:54,989 --> 00:04:00,560
Each agent that the host offers becomes something the assistant can call.

50
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:05,555
Under Agents, tick the agents of this site that the assistant may call.

51
00:04:05,555 --> 00:04:08,560
Always-available agents are already included.

52
00:04:09,015 --> 00:04:10,885
Click Save.

53
00:04:15,071 --> 00:04:17,516
Now ask a question for the specialist:

54
00:04:17,516 --> 00:04:19,461
what does the warranty cover?

55
00:04:19,911 --> 00:04:25,721
The assistant hands the question to the Warranty Agent, and answers with what the agent returned.

56
00:04:29,921 --> 00:04:31,150
Specialists:

57
00:04:31,150 --> 00:04:37,771
a legal, finance or warranty agent that answers in its own area, with its own instructions.

58
00:04:38,521 --> 00:04:39,423
Partners:

59
00:04:39,423 --> 00:04:44,351
a supplier or a sister company offers an agent, and your assistants call it.

60
00:04:45,101 --> 00:04:45,918
Reuse:

61
00:04:45,918 --> 00:04:51,771
one agent serves many assistants, so you maintain its instructions in one place.

62
00:04:52,521 --> 00:04:53,285
Care:

63
00:04:53,285 --> 00:04:59,121
describe each agent precisely, and give an assistant only the agents it needs.

64
00:05:01,121 --> 00:05:06,518
Create specialist agents, offer them with the A2A Host, and connect to the

65
00:05:06,518 --> 00:05:08,542
agents of other systems.

66
00:05:08,542 --> 00:05:12,927
Your assistants then hand each job to the right specialist.

67
00:05:12,927 --> 00:05:14,681
Thanks for watching.

